docs/*
!docs/*.md

# Internal handoff doc — agent-to-agent context, not for public eyes.
# Held back even though it's an .md.
docs/HANDOFF.md

# Ghidra-derived decompiled C from Sacred.exe — keep local only.
# Modders don't need it; RE hackers can regenerate from Sacred.exe
# + the Java scripts in re/ghidra/.
re/ghidra/decompiled/

SacredStudio/obj

# ReBorn-derived analysis artifacts. The ADDRESS MAP (reborn_symbols.json) and the
# hand-curated symbol list stay: they are interoperability facts about where things
# live, and contain no third-party code. Everything below is disassembled or copied
# bytes from someone else's binary and is regenerated locally by
# re/py/x86/reborn_catalog.py from the user's own SacredReborn.exe.
re/reborn_patch_sites.txt
re/reborn_patch_sites.json
re/hd_table.gen.json
re/hd_golden.inc
re/patch_review_queue.md
patchset/records_generated.inc
hd/hd_table.inc

# The Lua framework at custom/ IS the product and is tracked -- except the
# vanilla script dumps under it: those are decompiled game data, the same policy
# as Sacred_decrypted.exe and re/ghidra/decompiled. Regenerate them locally from
# your own install; never redistribute.
custom/lua/_vanilla/*
!custom/lua/_vanilla/README.md

